                  </p>
                  </div>
                  <div class="context-panel" data-panel="ai" hidden>
                    <strong>
                      AI-assisted option
                    </strong>
                    <p>
                      Give AI the labelled raw data, the fixed normalisation boundaries, the fitting commands, and the held-back commands. Ask it to preserve the raw columns, add derived \(x\) and \(v\) columns, and compare linear, quadratic, and power-law candidates using the same rows, residual definition, and error metric.
                    </p>
                    <div class="prompt-snippet">
                      “Preserve these raw PWM and settled-speed measurements. Using my stated usable-range boundaries, add normalised \(x\) and \(v\) columns. Fit linear, quadratic, and power-law models to the same fitting rows; report coefficients, uncertainty, residuals, and MAE; then evaluate the frozen models on these held-back commands. Do not invent values or interpret a fitted equation as a hidden motor mechanism.”
